# Codex cost cache CPU on a large local history
#
# Corpus: a copy of one real Codex cost cache (46,481 session files, 1,075,554 usage rows,
# 959 MB SQLite) against the matching ~/.codex sessions (63 GB of JSONL, read-only).
# Harness: Scripts/StoreStress, release build with -enable-testing, run from a disposable
# cache copy. Each PASS mirrors one UsageStore.runCodexCostCatchUp iteration.
# 'cpu' is process CPU time; counters come from CostUsageStoreReadWorkRecorder.

