## Regular token refresh (storestress refresh <copy> ~/.codex 3 30), warm passes
# Before: each refresh escalated to a full .report read (~1.07M row decodes, ~30s CPU) plus a full scan load.
  refresh 2 cpu=21.08s scannerSnapshots=0 usageRows=268541 rowDecodes=268541 readViewConversions=2 integrityChecks=0
  refresh 3 cpu=22.18s scannerSnapshots=0 usageRows=269666 rowDecodes=269666 readViewConversions=2 integrityChecks=0
# 30-day token and cost totals were identical across every refresh.

## Windowed report reads equal full report reads (storestress reportcompare <copy> <days>)
REPORTCOMPARE days=7   fullRead=10.44s windowedRead=2.24s dailyMatch=true projectsMatch=true sessionsMatch=true
REPORTCOMPARE days=30  fullRead=10.22s windowedRead=3.96s dailyMatch=true projectsMatch=true sessionsMatch=true
REPORTCOMPARE days=90  fullRead=16.24s windowedRead=8.20s dailyMatch=true projectsMatch=true sessionsMatch=true
REPORTCOMPARE days=365 fullRead=10.43s windowedRead=9.25s dailyMatch=true projectsMatch=true sessionsMatch=true
# Project costs are compared to 1/100 cent: Double sums built in dictionary order differ in the last bits
# even between two reads of one unchanged view.

## Installed app on the same machine (5-minute refresh, Codex cost tracking and storage usage enabled)
# 0.65.0 release: 158:56 CPU over 4h44m (56% average), 90-100% sustained in samples, RSS 10.8 GB.
#   During that run its retention evicted the cache from 46,481 to 1,555 files (603 -> 173 aggregate days).
# This branch, packaged locally, first 20 minutes on that evicted cache (re-adding history each refresh):
#   0% between refreshes, one 16-30s burst per 5-minute refresh, 82s CPU total (~7% average), RSS <= 1.1 GB.
